WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.793
Hi, friends.

00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:15.449
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:19.173
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:22.897
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.622
This is the Problem-Solving Four.

00:00:26.622 --> 00:00:35.001
When something goes wrong, there are four steps that can help. We take them in order, one at a time.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:41.519
First, stop and breathe. Second, say the problem in words. Third, think of choices. Fourth, pick one and try it.

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:54.554
Step one: stop and breathe. Let's practice with a pretend problem — your block tower just fell down. Hands still. One slow breath in… and let it go.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:01:07.589
Step two: say the problem in words. Just the facts: "My tower fell down." Words make a problem small enough to hold.

00:01:07.589 --> 00:01:20.624
Step three: think of choices. There is almost always more than one. "I can build it again. I can build it smaller. I can ask a friend to help."

00:01:20.624 --> 00:01:33.659
Step four: pick one… and try it. Picking one is enough. If it doesn't work, that's okay — you can go back and pick another.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:42.970
Four steps, in order: stop and breathe… say it in words… think of choices… pick one and try it. They're yours now — for any problem, big or small.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.832
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:01:44.832 --> 00:01:48.556
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:52.281
You're ready for what's next.
